You might want to check out R Shiny:
http://www.rstudio.com/shiny/

RStudio offers beta access to hosting, which is very simple to use:
https://rstudio.wufoo.com/forms/shiny-server-beta-program/

Otherwise, you can configure the R Shiny server on an EC2 instance
following various walkthroughs:
http://www.r-bloggers.com/deploying-shiny-server-on-amazon-ec2/
http://stackoverflow.com/questions/5187338/public-amazon-ec2-amis-with-r-pre-installed

